const VIVA=[
 ["Why is a matching result meaningful only when the tradition and profile are named?","Different traditions use different factor lists, tables, thresholds and exceptions. Without the profile, nobody can reproduce or check the result."],
 ["A pair scores 30 of 36 but has Nadi Dosha. How do you report it?","Report the total, list the Nadi Dosha as identified, test each exception rule against its conditions, state that none is verified or applied, keep the raw score, and add the chart layers separately."],
 ["A pair scores 15 of 36 and the charts look supportive. What do you say?","The Koota result stays 15 under the profile used. Supportive chart observations are recorded in their own layer; they do not rewrite the Koota result. Both are explained and the choice stays with the individuals."],
 ["How do you handle an approximate birth time?","State the accuracy, compute the Moon at both ends of the time range, report whether a Pada or Nakshatra boundary is crossed, and mark Lagna-dependent findings as uncertain."],
 ["Two software tools show different Nakshatras for the same person. What do you check?","Ayanamsha, Moon longitude, time-zone and daylight-saving handling, boundary precision, and whether the tools use the same Nakshatra and Pada rules. Astronomical differences are separated from rule differences."],
 ["What is the difference between a Dosha and a score deficiency?","A flagged Dosha is a condition the tradition names (for example same Nadi); a score deficiency is only a lower number in a Koota. A deficiency need not be an independent Dosha."],
 ["Explain the difference between cancellation and mitigation.","Cancellation means a named source states that the Dosha does not operate under defined conditions. Mitigation means other factors support the pair while the Dosha remains."],
 ["When may points be restored after a cancellation?","Only when the selected profile explicitly authorises it. Even then the adjusted score is labelled adjusted and the raw score stays visible."],
 ["A client asks you to say whether the marriage will succeed. What do you answer?","No horoscope can guarantee an outcome. Explain what each layer shows, what it cannot show, and the practical matters the two people should discuss."],
 ["Why must Rajju and Vedha not be added to the 36-point total?","In Tradition A they are pass or Dosha checks with no points. Adding points would invent a scoring rule."],
 ["What does it mean that Taurus–Libra is 6/8 and not 6/6?","Counts of different signs always add to 14, so one direction is 6 and the other is 8."],
 ["How do you treat Mahendra and Stree Deergha in a Tradition A report?","They are supplementary regional factors, shown separately and outside the 36-point total, with the threshold variant stated."],
 ["A client follows the Tamil Pathu Porutham. What do you do?","Use the documented provisional profile, show qualifying factors out of ten, state that it is not comparable with 36 points, and state which parts of the profile are unverified."],
 ["What may you say about Telugu, Kannada and Kerala profiles in this course?","That regional practice is documented, but a sufficiently verified independent rule profile is not yet established; the profile is marked pending research."],
 ["What is the role of D-9 in your report?","It is a supplementary chart: it adds context about dignity and the seventh house, but it does not replace D-1 and does not cancel a Koota Dosha."],
 ["How is the D-9 sign of a longitude calculated?","Navamsha index = floor(longitude / 3°20') mod 12, with 0 = Aries, using the sidereal longitude."],
 ["Why can a D-1 strong and D-9 weak planet not be summarised as good or bad?","Each chart says something different; the report states both and what needs qualification, without letting one erase the other."],
 ["What do you do when one person's seventh lord is friendly to the other's but not mutually?","Report the two directions separately; one-sided friendship is not mutual friendship."],
 ["What is the limit of the Vimshottari reading in your report?","It is a timing observation for the declared year-length convention; it is not an event date and does not change the Koota result."],
 ["How do you present a transit?","As a practitioner-entered observation read together with the natal promise and the Dasha, never alone."],
 ["What practical matters must always be left to the two people?","Communication, expectations, finances, family responsibilities, living arrangements, lifestyle, boundaries, long-term goals and mutual consent."],
 ["How do you respond when another astrologer reached a different result?","Compare the settings and rules, not the people. Show where the calculation or the tradition differs, and keep both results visible."],
 ["How should an error found after issuing a report be handled?","Correct it transparently: issue a new version with the change recorded; do not alter the issued report silently."],
 ["What must be in the audit before a report is issued?","Birth data, offset, ayanamsha, Moon, Nakshatra, Pada, Koota scores, D-1 and D-9, Dasha, aspects, rule sources, evidence levels, disclaimers and absence of absolute claims."],
 ["Why is there no combined compatibility percentage?","The layers measure different things on different scales; adding them would invent a formula that no source defines."],
 ["What is the correct statement about Nadi Dosha and health?","Nadi Dosha is a traditional classification derived from the Nakshatra. It is not a genetic or medical finding and cannot diagnose anything."],
 ["How do you explain a Gana mismatch responsibly?","As a symbolic classification result under the selected table, with the Dosha flag rule stated, and not as a statement about anyone's temperament or conduct."],
 ["A client wants a remedy for every Dosha. What is your position?","A remedy is an optional personal practice; nothing in the report claims that it changes an outcome, and no one should be pressured."],
 ["How do you keep client data confidential?","Use case identifiers, record only necessary details, share a report only with the people concerned and with their permission."],
 ["What does 'identified, not applied' mean?","The exception category exists and its conditions may be met, but no verified source attaches to it, so the status of the Dosha is unchanged."],
 ["How would you tell a student who used a different recognised school that they are wrong?","I would not. A different documented school applied correctly and disclosed is acceptable; the marking checks method, disclosure and consistency."]];
